kosha gas

  -- no definite shape and no definite volume. fills its container completely.
  -- atoms/molecules move freely and rapidly — translational, rotational, vibrational.
  -- thermal energy >> intermolecular forces (except near condensation).
  -- compressible: volume changes significantly with pressure and temperature.
  --
  -- ideal gas law: PV = nRT
  --   P = pressure (Pa), V = volume (m³), n = moles, R = 8.314 J/mol·K, T = kelvin.
  -- at standard conditions: 1 mol ideal gas occupies 22.4 L.
  -- real gases deviate: van der Waals equation adds intermolecular forces and volume.
  --
  -- kinetic theory: gas pressure = force per unit area from molecular collisions.
  -- average kinetic energy = (3/2)kT — temperature IS average molecular KE.
  -- Maxwell-Boltzmann distribution: spread of molecular speeds at given temperature.
  --
  -- properties:
  --   low density: ~1000x less dense than liquid at same temperature.
  --   diffusion: gases mix spontaneously (entropy drives it).
  --   effusion: gas escapes through small hole — rate ∝ 1/√(molar mass). Graham's law.
  --
  -- in 3d / pratibimba: volume rendering — participating medium, smoke, fog shader.
  -- transparent to semi-transparent. scatters light (Rayleigh → blue sky).

